<title>POLAND: NFI Progress revises down 1996 results.</title>
<headline>NFI Progress revises down 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish National Investment Fund No 4 or Progress had a net loss of 32 million zlotys in 1996, against 3.6 million zloty net loss in 1995, the fund said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Earlier Progress said it had a net loss of 11.5 million zlotys in 1996.</p>
<p>Under the government's NFI programme, shares in about 500 mid-sized companies are allocated to 15 NFIs run by foreign and domestic management firms. @</p>
<p>From May 12, the 26 million Poles who bought participation units in the scheme have been able to exchange each of them for 15 shares, one in each fund. On Thursday, shares of the funds will start trade on the Warsaw bourse.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
